# The stated limits of Traceworks, as the judge of the security self-audit gets them: what the documentation says
# the defaults do not protect. A behaviour a limit states is not a finding; code that does more than the limit says is.
# The format is described in the package's README.md ("What the judge is told"). A test pins this file to the
# documents: every heading and every bullet of "What they do not protect" in docs/security.md is named here, in the
# documents' order, as a limit or as an aside (a point that says nothing about what the code does); each entry names
# the digest of its bullet's whole text, so any change of a bullet fails the test; and every quote is in its bullet.
# A limit that stands elsewhere, among the guarantees ("What the defaults protect") or in another document, is named
# by the bold lead of its passage, and the digest covers the whole passage. A "says" line may narrow its bullet, never
# widen it: it keeps every bound the bullet sets. The numbered list in the instructions of workflow.json is made from
# the "says" lines, and a test holds the two together.
#
# Asides, and why: "Claude as root" (Claude refuses every tool level above none then, so the step fails and gains
# nothing), "A prompt that starts with /" (Claude answers that the command is not available: a reply, no action),
# "Codex is not supported" (refused), "The private key is yours to keep" (Traceworks never reads it), and the two
# seal points that say what a seal means, not what the code does.

source docs/security.md

section What the defaults protect

limit Mounts.
  quote a folder with a credential store of its own (`.ssh`, `.aws`, ...) is not refused
  says  A workspace or a package is refused when it is, or holds, the runs, ledger, registers, seals or cache folder (also where a setting puts them), but may lie elsewhere in the Traceworks home or in a folder of /dev/shm, and is not refused for holding a credential store of its own (.ssh, .aws); a block's own mount stays under the whole mount check.
  digest e2ee679333d09bc2

limit Hooks
  quote with the operator's whole environment
  quote the tail of its standard error, unredacted, so a hook must not print a secret
  says  A hook is the operator's code, set in traceworks.json and never by a workflow: it runs on the host without a shell, with the operator's whole environment, gets only the register's diff, and the tail of its standard error goes to the register's log and page unredacted.
  digest 84bf8d1ffc3c5b8c

limit Registers
  quote Lines appended after the last anchor are accepted.
  quote But they can **add** to both
  says  A line appended to a register's log after its last anchor is accepted and named as unproven until the next write anchors it; whoever can write both the register's folder and the ledger can add a forged decision with its anchor without a trace, though not rewrite one unnoticed: decisions are not signed.
  digest 40eaf5ab88ded69a

limit The register folder of a run
  quote In a host run nothing keeps a command from writing the folder
  quote An audit package you run is trusted with the names of the people who decided on its findings.
  says  In a host run nothing keeps a command from writing the run's register folder: it is compared with the recorded digests before each command that gets it, not while it reads; in a container run it is a read-only mount. Every shell and tool step of an audit can read it, who decided included; an AI step's container does not get it.
  digest 2f557af3549e9794

limit What nothing in this version finds:
  quote the ledger is not signed
  quote a record cut to its first line
  says  The ledger check does not find what was before a new ledger, a well-formed entry or acknowledgement committed by hand (the ledger is not signed), a record cut to its first line, or an audit run in a place this ledger does not see; what the bullets before it list is found.
  digest 5d1d25922cbb8aad

section AI steps

limit Who chooses the model of an AI step.
  quote without `allowed_models`, any package may name any model of a provider you hold a credential for
  says  The workflow names the model of an AI step, and a caller can pick only among the options its model_choices declares; without allowed_models a package may name any model of a provider the operator holds a credential for, and a step without a model runs the provider's default.
  digest 7f7fa65b24b6c5f7

limit A local model
  quote "Local" is what you declared, not what Traceworks verified.
  says  A local model server is what the operator declared in local_models, which no workflow widens, and is not verified: Traceworks sees only its host:port, plain HTTP to it is not encrypted, and with an older Docker or with Podman an AI container can reach a server on the host past the proxy. The call still gets no provider credential.
  digest 36149ff6fecc22c2

limit `ai_images` replaces the built-in image.
  quote Traceworks never builds, pulls or inspects it
  says  An image the operator sets in ai_images (no package and no environment variable sets it) gets the credentials, the workspace, the prompt and the network of the built-in image, and is never built, pulled or inspected.
  digest 42bfd202f442df07

limit An AI container reaches its provider, and everything a model reads goes there.
  quote The allowlist limits where a container can connect, not what the model sends to the host it may reach
  says  The allowlist limits where an AI container connects, not what the model sends there: the prompt, the files its tools read and their output go to the provider.
  digest 69af24556038d833

limit What the allowlist closes, and what it leaves.
  quote The proxy sees only `host:port`, never which account a connection serves.
  says  The egress proxy closes the open network for an AI container but judges host:port only and inspects no TLS: the provider's host, under any account, and every host of ai_hosts stay reachable, a denied connection is recorded and fails no step, and with ai_network open nothing is refused or recorded.
  digest 7cf9a97fdf51a0c8

limit Web tools
  quote The proxy sees and records only `host:port`, never the URL
  says  Web tools are off unless a block sets them and the workflow declares ai.web; then a fetched URL or a search query can carry what the model read to a host of web_hosts or to the provider, the injection check is a tripwire, and a host listed by name gets no address check (the star refuses private addresses and every port but 443).
  digest 3d0703747c36037d

limit A model with tools can read its own credential.
  quote The record redacts the key, but the model can put it into its answer, which later steps of the run see as it is.
  says  A model with tools can read its own API key in its container and put it into its answer, which later steps see unredacted; the record redacts it, and the container reaches no host but its provider's.
  digest 5eae424f060efbba

limit A model's answer in a shell command.
  quote Traceworks guarantees that the value is in the variable and nowhere in the code.
  quote What the prompt shows, the person has seen and answers for.
  says  Traceworks never writes a protected value into shell code: it reaches a shell step as a variable (values), and Traceworks guarantees that the value is in the variable and nowhere in the code. What the author's command does with the variable is the author's: unquoted, evaluated or exported it can run or leak a model's text. A default taken at the console with an empty line is a person's answer only when the prompt showed it whole.
  digest 9a72496d9c717b7c

limit A gate from an AI step.
  quote a model steered by what it reads can therefore set a gate too
  says  A simple or agentic step can set the run's gate with a gate_status line at the start of a line, so a model can; the output of a foreach, retry, while or conditional in AI mode sets no gate.
  digest e3a31960f2fa66ac

aside Claude as root.
  digest 374c2371f5ef8d91
aside A prompt that starts with `/`.
  digest a134c1529ec11956

limit Pi as root.
  quote Pi runs as root with every tool its step allows
  says  Containers run as the owner of the Traceworks home: when that is root, Pi runs as root in its container with every tool its step allows, and nothing refuses that.
  digest 984205832311ab33

limit Pi with a Claude subscription token
  quote presents itself to Anthropic as Claude Code
  says  Pi given a Claude subscription token (ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_TOKEN, or an sk-ant-oat value in ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) presents itself to Anthropic as Claude Code; that is Pi's own behaviour, and Traceworks hands it the credential as stored.
  digest 55d43e52c4edaa61

limit Pi and a writable workspace.
  quote but it renames a `.pi/commands/` folder there to `.pi/prompts/` when it starts
  says  With workspace_writable true Pi applies nothing of the workspace's .pi/, but renames a .pi/commands/ folder there to .pi/prompts/ when it starts, and a step before it can have written that folder.
  digest 187843673cc5a1b8

aside Codex is not supported.
  digest 3761c530818c6962

section Secrets and the record

limit Redaction is exact-match only.
  quote Redaction keeps accidents out of the record; it does not stop a step that means to leak.
  says  Redaction finds a secret value byte for byte: a value that a step or a model writes encoded, split, escaped or reversed is recorded readably. A value as Traceworks itself writes it into the record (lines, blobs, cuts) is still redacted.
  digest 924e9f3d76bb30a0

limit A step can do anything with its secret.
  quote with `network: true` the command can send it anywhere
  says  Only the step that declares a secret gets it: that step holds it as an environment variable and can do anything with it, also send it out with network: true. A step that did not declare it must not get it.
  digest 58c5ce185aec1a8d

limit The scratch directory keeps what steps wrote, in plain text.
  quote a file there that holds a secret is listed without its content, but the file stays
  says  The scratch directory of a run folder is not part of the record and keeps what steps wrote, secrets included, in plain text; in the record a scratch file that holds a secret is listed without its content.
  digest 08dd459ed9c83042

limit The inbox keeps what you sent a running run, in plain text.
  quote `inbox/done/` is not part of the record and is not redacted
  says  The inbox of a run folder (inbox/done/) keeps answers and comments as they were typed, unredacted; the record redacts them.
  digest 747f85a7a87abc66

limit Later steps read what a step wrote.
  quote is there for every later container of the run
  says  What a step writes into /scratch or a writable workspace is readable by every later step of the run, AI steps and host commands included.
  digest 4b7419c121e31a5d

limit An answer to a parked run is redacted like the rest of the record.
  quote a secret you typed that is not one of the run's is recorded as typed
  says  An answer to a parked run is redacted with the run's declared secrets and the credentials of its AI providers as they are then; any other secret typed into it is recorded as typed.
  digest 2f7b3bf84ffcc14d

limit A resume redacts with the values it has at the resume.
  quote the resumed run knows only the new one
  says  A resume redacts with the secret values it reads at the resume: an old value that changed while the run stood and that a later step prints is recorded in clear; the warning compares only the modification time of credentials.json.
  digest 9ccbdf881d327d90

limit The runtime shows a container's environment.
  quote the `docker` or `podman` client process holds them in its own environment
  says  While a container runs, its environment, secret values included, is shown to whoever may use the runtime, and the docker or podman client process holds them in its environment; they are never on a command line.
  digest ae1bfd78ca32ddc2

limit The record is tamper-evident, not signed.
  quote Whoever can write the Traceworks home can rewrite a run folder and its ledger entries together, the start entry too.
  says  Manifests are not signed (only seals are): whoever can write the Traceworks home can rewrite a run folder and its ledger entries together; verify finds a change that does not rewrite both.
  digest 16bdddf4be3dcc47

limit The places are the operator's.
  quote It does not know a folder that an earlier value of a setting named
  says  runs_dir, ledger_dir and registers_dir are read from traceworks.json only and checked as written; the mount check on real paths covers the folders they name and those of the home, not a folder an earlier value of a setting named.
  digest fc8fb416acb6aadc

section Seals

limit An unsealed package runs, unless you say otherwise.
  quote Only `require_seal: "always"` stops that.
  says  By default a seal binds only the packages that have one: an unsealed package runs unless require_seal is always, and a sealed one becomes unsealed by deleting traceworks.seal and changing the workflow id; a sealed workflow id without its seal is refused.
  digest 33b3f7f42cfa91bf

limit `require_seal: "unattended"` guards against accidents, not against a caller.
  quote Whoever starts the run can pass the flag or give the command a terminal.
  says  require_seal unattended refuses an unsealed package only without a terminal and without --allow-unsealed; whoever starts the run can give either.
  digest d9d0cea03619c678

limit The `signer` of a seal is a declared name.
  quote nobody checks who that is
  says  The signer of a seal is a declared name nobody checks; the key, its fingerprint and the names allowed_signers gives it are checked.
  digest f9043520416df4af

limit What the digest does not see.
  quote A change there breaks no seal.
  quote It does not hold for the hashed short name NTFS gives `.git`
  says  The seal digest does not see an empty directory, a file that is not a regular file, permission bits other than the owner's execute bit, or the top-level .git/ in the spellings a file system may take for it, except the hashed short name NTFS can give .git; a change of anything else in the package breaks the seal.
  digest 8418778ab5ebe33d

limit A called package is loaded again when its block runs.
  quote A called package changed in between runs changed.
  quote a called package that lies in the workspace can be rewritten by a step
  says  A called package is checked when the run starts and resumes and loaded again when its block runs, without a comparison: changed in between, also by a step of the run in a writable workspace, it runs changed with the run's secrets. A workflow an unsealed package names through a placeholder is not checked at all.
  digest d915a69a5099ee69

limit Whoever writes the home is the operator.
  quote What is not guarded is what the settings do not name
  says  Whoever can write the home (traceworks.json, allowed_signers, the seal log) is the operator and can allow a key or switch seals off. No container gets these from Traceworks: a step's mount inside the home is refused, and a signing_key or allowed_signers outside the home is guarded where it lies; the public half of the key and a key passed with seal --key are not.
  digest fb07bd7c3d783592

limit The end of the seal log is not anchored.
  quote It does not show lines cut from the end.
  says  The chain of the seal log shows a changed or removed line in the middle, not lines cut from its end; the seal file in the package is still checked.
  digest dce1d63b73dcf9a9

limit An allowed signer can seal anything.
  quote A package sealed again by any key in `allowed_signers` runs
  says  A package sealed again by any key of allowed_signers runs, also when this home sealed another digest before.
  digest 2ea56cdc717bbcb4

limit An earlier seal put back is refused, as far as the log remembers.
  quote a home that never saw the workflow takes any valid seal
  says  An earlier valid seal put back is refused only when the seal log remembers a later change for its workflow: a home that never saw the workflow, or a log cut at its end, takes it; the rule compares the signer's own signed time with this home's clock.
  digest d97d1a4a7da49740

limit `unseal` is not signed.
  quote Anyone who may run `traceworks unseal` in the home removes a seal
  says  unseal is not signed: anyone who may run it in the home removes a seal, and the log names them; seal_immutable switches the command off.
  digest 5ac9634c0dab06be

aside The private key is yours to keep.
  digest 5e81f15962bc4640

limit Images are fixed as far as their names go.
  quote The built image is not sealed
  says  A sealed package must name registry images and the images of its Dockerfiles by digest; an image a Dockerfile reaches another way (a build argument, a download), the built image, the built-in images and ai_images are not sealed.
  digest 916dc321268c5c74

limit The workspace and the source are not sealed.
  quote The seal says which package runs, not what it works on.
  says  The seal says which package runs, not what it works on: the workspace and a --source are not sealed; a --source is pinned to a commit in the record.
  digest 5b7431e7612a9458

limit A file changed after the start is not seen.
  quote a file changed while the run is going reaches the later steps
  says  The seal digest is taken at the start and at a resume, and a step mounts the package as it is when the step starts: a package file changed while the run is going reaches the later steps, which see it read-only.
  digest 1edfb66c8ee22fba

aside A seal says who signed, not that the package is good.
  digest c7f81e7ea437dbec
aside A seal holds where its signer is allowed.
  digest 11bc690d1979839a

section Child workflows

limit A child workflow is not a boundary.
  quote Nothing a parent does keeps a child from a file
  says  A child workflow is part of the run that started it: the same workspace, scratch directory, networks, credentials and variables, the protected ones still protected.
  digest 0135e95d5fa2167b

limit The parent's package decides which workflows run.
  quote whoever writes the package, or picks such an input, picks the code that runs with the run's secrets and workspace
  says  A workflow_id is a path below the package or a workflow id, written out or filled in from a trusted variable, an input of the run included, never from a protected value: whoever writes the package or picks that input picks the code that runs.
  digest b3b22b6d031325df

limit A child's gate does not reach the run.
  quote leaves its parent `COMPLETED` without a gate unless a step of the parent states the verdict
  says  A child's gate or errors do not reach the parent run unless a step of the parent states the verdict.
  digest d45455e2f2dd328e

section Images and containers

limit A package image's `RUN` steps run at build time.
  quote with network and without the flags a run's containers get
  says  traceworks images build runs a package's Dockerfile RUN steps at build time, with network and without the flags of a run's containers, and pulls the registry images the package names.
  digest eaabff565b0e7d02

limit A tag names the Dockerfile's directory, not the image's bytes.
  quote A rebuild on another day can differ under the same tag.
  says  An image tag names the Dockerfile's directory, not the image's bytes: a rebuild can differ under the same tag; the record names the image ID each container started from.
  digest b6b9c3a74cf7b99d

limit The budget counts what a run holds, not each copy of it.
  quote Checkpoints are not bounded by the budget
  says  The output budget does not count the short-lived copies of an output, and checkpoints are not bounded by it: a run needs a heap of about three times its budget.
  digest 602239eae0d3be0d

limit The check of a mount's container side is textual.
  quote is refused by its path as written
  says  A declared mount on or below /workspace, /package or /scratch is refused by its container path as written: a symbolic link inside the image can still land a mount elsewhere on one of them.
  digest 2e7c760d86e71551

limit A mount is checked, then mounted.
  quote a process that can write one of its parent directories could still swap a part of it in between
  says  The host side of a mount is resolved once and the runtime gets the checked real path; a process that can write a parent directory of it can still swap a part before the runtime opens it.
  digest b988183568735c9d

limit A writable mount below the home.
  quote it does not refuse a writable mount (`:rw`) of any other file or folder of yours
  says  The mount check refuses the home as a whole, the logins below it and the places it lists, not a writable mount of any other file or folder of the operator, such as ~/.bashrc or the .git/hooks of a repository.
  digest b28ca8938a975d2d

limit A writable workspace has its own `.git`.
  quote With `workspace_writable: true` a step writes everything in the workspace, its `.git/` included
  quote Traceworks does not cover or check the workspace's `.git`
  says  With workspace_writable: true a step writes everything in the workspace, its own .git included (hooks, config), which Traceworks neither covers nor checks: the next git command the operator runs in that directory on the host runs what the step left there, as the operator.
  digest ba84cb6fcb578128

limit A called package's `.git` in the workspace.
  quote has no cover while the steps of the calling package run
  says  The package's own .git is covered wherever a container sees the package, and a workspace that lies inside it is refused; the .git of a package it calls that lies in the workspace has no cover while the steps of the calling package run, which see it as any file of the workspace.
  digest 8f118109e20af8a4

limit The tool caches are shared between runs.
  quote What one run's tool wrote there, a later run's tool reads.
  says  A tool step's cache folder (cache_dir) belongs to an image name and is shared by every package that names that image: what one run's tool wrote, a later run's tool reads.
  digest d1b95d4374b7b9cd

limit Sockets, pipes and devices deeper down.
  quote but a folder with one of them two or more levels down is not
  says  A socket file, a named pipe, a device node and a folder that directly holds one are refused as a mount; a folder with one of them two or more levels down is not.
  digest c1c0e04ec2aa616d

limit Runtime storage elsewhere.
  quote is not refused as a mount
  says  The mount check knows the runtimes' default storage directories, not storage moved elsewhere (a data-root, a storage under XDG_DATA_HOME).
  digest ed9309f362dd493e

aside The container is as strong as the runtime and the kernel.
  digest d21be5877eda4b1e

section Many containers on a desktop machine

section The host and `--source`

limit A host run's commands run as you.
  quote they can read and change everything you can
  says  The commands of a host run, which needs the operator's consent and never runs while a container runtime answers, run as the operator and can read and change what the operator can; their environment is still reduced, without API keys and tokens.
  digest c7f9eee3da618609

limit git on the host gets a reduced environment.
  quote Your SSH agent and your credential helper stay reachable
  says  git runs on the host against files nobody checked, with a reduced environment that holds no GIT_ variable and no API key; the operator's SSH agent and credential helper stay reachable to it.
  digest a0c0072dd2a1a930

limit Patterns and reports are read under a time limit.
  quote the thread is left behind, busy until the Traceworks process ends
  quote it refuses some patterns the engine would match quickly
  says  A workflow's regular expression is matched under a time limit; a match that does not end leaves a busy thread behind until the process ends, and the check of a pattern's counts multiplies them all, so it refuses some patterns the engine would match quickly.
  digest 573d07610ab60212

limit A token in a `--source` URL
  quote every process on the machine can read it in the process list while the clone runs
  says  A token in a --source URL is an argument of git clone and readable in the process list while the clone runs.
  digest ba9cdb883ecadf7d

limit A gitfile that points into a checkout.
  quote do not use a directory that steps could write as a `--source`
  says  A local --source whose .git is a file that points into a run's checkout is not refused; planting one needs a write outside the checkout.
  digest fcc8425d5f452bda

limit A source path is checked, then cloned.
  quote git resolves the path again when it clones
  says  A local --source is judged on the path as it resolves at the check, and git resolves it again when it clones: a part of the path that does not exist yet can be made a link by a step of a run going on at that moment.
  digest d6ffbaf74bfd9549

limit Paths in a package.
  quote may name its workflow by any path on the machine
  says  A sub-workflow or foreach block may name its workflow by any path on the machine that the package itself writes; a path from a step's output or a model is untrusted input and never reaches workflow_id.
  digest ed6d5e86044d75dc

source docs/events.md

section Redaction

limit Lines:
  quote which must keep naming their blob
  says  Numbers, booleans and blob references (sha256 and size) in a line of the record are kept, not redacted; every other string of the line, a field called sha256 included, is redacted.
  digest 63c2fb90f40803e3
